      "reason": "qos_rate is not a shape of unifi.Client: three of its members are fields of a SEPARATE ClientGroup object and the client carries only the group's id. Reading them turns usergroup_id into the group's name and rates; writing them looks the group up by name, re-rates it when the limits differ, and CREATES it when nothing matches -- which is why the write half is in BeforeSend and not in Prefetch, where it would fire on every refresh. qos_rate.id is deliberately NOT claimed: it names usergroup_id, a field of the client itself, through the member's own structural_name, and the descriptor carries it in AlwaysWire. A member cannot be both claimed and self-describing -- that is the contradiction the compiler refuses, and it is right to.",
      "structural_names": [
